    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## What was required\n\n`POST /api/owners` may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner response must expose `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. The acceptance test creates an owner with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `salutation` = `\"DR who\"` \u2014 so the title has to persist across the create/reload.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` string to the `OwnerFields` input schema, and a read-only `salutation` string to the `Owner` output schema (DTOs are generated from this at build time).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n- **`rest/function/owner/Salutation.java`** (new) \u2014 helper deriving the salutation, following the existing `AgeBand`/`CustomerCode` helper pattern: returns `lastName` alone when the title is null/blank, else `title + \" \" + lastName`.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping expression (title itself maps automatically by name from `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2192 `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`).\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column. Tests run on the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema file drives the column.\n\nI kept `title` as a plain string rather than an enum to avoid MapStruct enum\u2194String conversion complexity; the description still documents the MR/MRS/MS/DR values.\n\n## Result\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes and the full `mvnw test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures/errors).",
